import { z } from 'zod';
export const getAuthenticationGuideSchema = z.object({});
export function handleGetAuthenticationGuide() {
    return `# Authentication Guide

## Endpoint

\`\`\`
https://api.onesource.io/federation/{chain}/graphql
\`\`\`

Replace \`{chain}\` with the target blockchain slug:

| Chain | Slug |
|-------|------|
| Ethereum | \`ethereum\` |
| Base | \`base\` |
| Optimism | \`optimism\` |
| Avalanche | \`avax\` |
| Shape | \`shape\` |
| Sepolia (testnet) | \`sepolia\` |

## API Key

All requests require an API key via the \`x-bp-token\` HTTP header:

\`\`\`
x-bp-token: BP-{YOUR_API_KEY}
\`\`\`

**Key format:** \`BP-\` prefix followed by 24 alphanumeric characters (e.g. \`BP-12345678912345678912345678\`).

**Getting a key:**
1. Sign up at [app.onesource.io](https://app.onesource.io)
2. Navigate to your dashboard
3. Create a new API key

## Quick Test

\`\`\`bash
curl -X POST "https://api.onesource.io/federation/ethereum/graphql" \\
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\
  -H "x-bp-token: BP-YOUR_API_KEY" \\
  -d '{"query": "{ block(number: 19000000) { number timestamp } }"}'
\`\`\`

If you get a JSON response with \`data.block\`, your key is working.

## Common Mistakes

| Mistake | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Using \`Authorization: Bearer\` | Use \`x-bp-token\` header instead |
| Key starts with \`sk_\` | OneSource keys start with \`BP-\` |
| Per-chain API keys | One key works across **all** chains |
| Missing \`Content-Type\` | Always send \`Content-Type: application/json\` |

## Subscription Plans

| Plan | Rate Limit | Notes |
|------|-----------|-------|
| Free | Limited queries/day | Good for testing and development |
| Starter | Higher rate limit | Production use |
| Pro | Highest rate limit | Enterprise workloads |

Manage your plan at [app.onesource.io](https://app.onesource.io).`;
}
